<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center;font-size:13px;color:#999;margin-bottom:20px;">The following summary and diagram are not part of the original text.</p>

<p class="no-indent" style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;">This halacha maps the final sections of the morning davening onto a single grand theme from LM II:2: <b>drawing the simchah and kedushah of Shabbos into the six weekdays</b>, thereby revealing <i>achdus haPashut</i> (the simple Unity of HaKadosh Baruch Hu) within the multiplicity of the world.</p>

<p class="no-indent" style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;margin-top:10px;">The key mechanism: <b>Halachos</b> ג†’ reveal truth ג†’ complete the <b>dibbur</b> ג†’ achieve <b>Lashon HaKodesh</b> (connected to Shabbos) ג†’ draw Shabbos-simchah into weekdays ג†’ all diverse actions included in the One.</p>

