<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center;font-size:20px;color:#7a622e;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:5px;">Translator's Overview</p>
<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center;font-size:13px;color:#999;margin-bottom:20px;">The following summary and diagram are not part of the original text.</p>

<p class="no-indent" style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;">This halacha, the longest in the entire collection, builds a single grand structure: the <b>N'kudah</b> (the holy point within each person = the Tzaddik = the holy love) must be bound to the heart. This IS tefillah. Bircas Kohanim at the end of tefillah is the culmination ג€” the holy love (Kohain) illuminates the heart. The four sections of davening correspond to four dimensions of the M'lapum ג€” four ways the N'kudah (yud) connects to the heart/world (vav).</p>

