<p class="no-indent" style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;">This section transitions from the structure of tefillah to <b>Kri'as HaTorah</b>. ֲ§21ג€“22 complete the davening sequence: the Shir shel Yom connects all worlds to the N'kudah through melody (each day has its unique N'kudah drawn from Shabbos). ֲ§23ג€“25 present one of Reb Noson's most powerful teachings: every public Torah reading is a re-enactment of Matan Torah, rectifying shivray Luchos. "Nosain haTorah" ג€” present tense ג€” means Torah is given anew constantly. The churban came because they treated Torah as a mere code of law ("shelo bairchu baTorah t'chilah"). ֲ§25 contains a startling passage on true Tzaddikim being sent in every generation to renew Torah. ֲ§26 links Bircas Kohanim to Bircas HaTorah. ֲ§27 reveals how the weekly Sidra guides each week ג€” seven parshiyos = seven days, the N'kudah personalized to each moment.</p>

