<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center;font-size:13px;color:#999;margin-bottom:20px;">The following summary and diagram are not part of the original text.</p>

<p class="no-indent" style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;">This concluding section maps the number of Torah readers to the intensity of the N'kudah's illumination on each day. The 39 melachos = tikkun sh'viras kailim caused by Adam HaRishon ג€” all elevated through sanctified work (M'leches HaMishkan). Yom Kippur = vav in ultimate completeness ג†’ receiving the yud (N'kudah of Shabbos) ג†’ second Luchos given ג†’ all avonos forgiven. Monday/Thursday readings trace to Moshe's ascent/descent for the second Luchos. Simchas Torah = all N'kudos of all Yisrael illuminating simultaneously = the ultimate simchah. ֲ§33 closes the grand circle: the numbers of Torah readers (3, 5, 7) correspond to Bircas Kohanim ג€” the holy love dwelling at the N'kudah ג€” with which the entire halacha began.</p>

